== Truncation Simulation
<apx-interpost-truncated>

Within-session gaps are only observable when the session is long enough to contain both posts: the observation process is $x | x < T$ with $T$ the session length (median $110$ s, p99 $1710$ s; see @tbl-cal-session-stats). To quantify what this does to family identification, `validate_truncated.R` simulates each candidate family, keeps the draws below a session-like ceiling $T$, and refits the survivors with the same untruncated candidates and AIC as the production pipeline (30 replicates per family, ceiling and sample size).

@tbl-apx-interpost-confusion shows the resulting confusion matrix at $n = 100$ (pooled over all ceilings): every light-tailed family is systematically classified as power-law in roughly a third to two thirds of replicates ---truncation manufactures power-law wins. The recovery table (@tbl-apx-interpost-acc) shows the ceiling dependence at both sample sizes: at $T <= 300$ s the light families sit at or below chance level, and even $n = 100$ observations do not help; they only separate at $T >= 900$ s. Since within gaps have p90 = 281 s, the whole within-session quantity lives in the unidentifiable regime and no within family composition is reportable (see @sec-cal-interpost).

