=== Per (Duration $times$ Gap) Pair

Restricting to (supposedly) homogeneous users makes the case stronger for a single parametric law. @tbl-apx-interpost-pooledpairs shows the AIC-best and AD-best per pair (the AD of the AIC winner in bold when catastrophic). The fit degenerates worse than pooled:

- *AIC and AD contradict each other in roughly 9 of 16 pairs.* Expon wins AIC in 8 pairs (the bulk is near-exponential), but its AD there is catastrophic (8k--93k, often the worst serious family): it fits the bulk and misses the tail, and AD weights exactly the tail. No winner is criterion-robust.
- *AD rejects everything everywhere.* Best AD across all pairs is $approx 161$ vs critical $approx 2.5$. Restricting to homogeneous users does not fix it: the session-ceiling kink exists inside every pair.
- *Winner identity is unstable across pairs* (gamma, weibull, expon, fisk and lognorm each win somewhere, several near-ties) although the shapes are visually near-identical: family choice is noise, not signal.

