=== Conclusion

The per-pair ECDFs already exist and are exactly the files the simulation loads (`results/within_ecdf__<dur>__<gap>.txt`, see @apx-interpost-pairs). A parametric law per pair is formally rejected everywhere and adds nothing the ECDF does not already encode exactly (burst floor, ceiling kink). The pair split is the finer-grained replacement for the coarser per-global-family ECDFs: the simulation assigns each user their (duration, gap) pair and loads the matching ECDF.

